                                      std::string* family_out);
 
+// The text-rasterisation tuple the composed persona carries, or nullopt when
+// no profile described the surface -- which is every stock launch and
+// `--fingerprint=host`.
+//
+// This exists so that the three platform implementations of
+// GetFontRenderParams above have ONE place to defer to. Each of them derives
+// the tuple from the host's own text engine -- the Windows shell's ClearType
+// settings, a constant that matches Skia's macOS defaults, the toolkit and
+// then fontconfig on Linux -- and a composed persona has to override all
+// three identically, because the value is read independently in the browser
+// (skia::LegacyDisplayGlobals and viz::GpuHostImpl::InitFontRenderParams from
+// BrowserMainLoop::PreMainMessageLoopRun), in the GPU process (viz), and in
+// every renderer (through blink::RendererPreferences). Overriding the one
+// function every one of them already calls is what makes those agree without
+// inventing a second delivery path for the same eight numbers.
+//
+// The profile keeps hinting and subpixel order as strings because base cannot
+// name a gfx enum; the mapping back is here, and it is total: the loader
+// refuses any other spelling, so there is no unknown string for this to
+// invent a value for.
+COMPONENT_EXPORT(GFX)
+std::optional<FontRenderParams> ComposedFontRenderParams();
